 settings. The generic text built from the email&#39;s subject is only for an email added later without its own text.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-booking-start-and-end" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booking start and end</h2><p class="gd-p">Every booking gets these by itself, by email, text and phone alert (each person&#39;s channel), once each, and again only when the time changes (an extension, a new pickup time):</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">When</th><th scope="col">The renter gets</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The day before pickup</td><td>What to bring, where and when</td></tr><tr><td>About 2 hours before pickup</td><td>&quot;See you at 2:00 pm today&quot;, the place and what to bring</td></tr><tr><td>30 minutes after a pickup nobody recorded</td><td>&quot;You&#39;re all set&quot;, the return time and place</td></tr><tr><td>The day before the return</td><td>The return time and place, fuel and keys</td></tr><tr><td>About 3 hours before the return</td><td>&quot;Your rental ends at 5:00 pm&quot;, fuel, clean, all keys and a one-tap Extend link</td></tr><tr><td>At the return time</td><td>&quot;Your booking ended at 5:00 pm&quot;, return now or extend</td></tr><tr><td>15 minutes late</td><td>T13, the late notice</td></tr><tr><td>2 hours late</td><td>T14, the final notice</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A booking whose pickup nobody recorded counts as out: it gets the end messages, the late notices and the late tasks like a rental on rent. Its status stays as it is.</li><li>The late notices and the short reminders go from 7 am to 10 pm. Overnight they wait until 7 am; a car returned in the night gets nothing.</li><li>The late panel&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Send T13</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Send T14</b> send the same notices: never twice.</li><li>An insurer-billed booking messages the renter too: they hold the car.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Pickup not recorded</b>: 30 minutes after the pickup time with nothing recorded, Fleet gets the task &quot;Record pickup for CC-xxxxx, or mark no-show&quot; and the field staff of the handover an alert and a text. At 3 hours the Admins get an alert and a task. They close by themselves once the pickup is recorded or the booking is cancelled.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Not back</b>: 15 minutes after the return time with no return recorded, the field staff of the return and the Admins get an alert and a text with the renter&#39;s name and phone, at any hour.</li><li>Each moment has its switch, all on: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Booking start and end&quot;. The text of each is in the list of texts on the same page.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-texts-a-day" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Texts a day</h2><p class="gd-p">Site health on <b class="gd-ui">To do</b> has <b class="gd-ui">Texts today</b>: sent, notifications among them, failed, not sent and sign-in codes for the last 7 days, and the texts waiting for 8 am.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-phone-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter, owner, investor and staff member can also get alerts on their phone or computer (web push), as well as their emails and texts. Each turns them on per device on their profile; the first page of each portal offers it once. On iPhone and iPad it works from the Home Screen app (Safari, <b class="gd-ui">Share</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add to Home Screen</b>; iOS 16.4 or later).</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>What alerts: new requests and offers, booking changes, payments, pickups and returns (field jobs), messages, urgent alerts and documents to sign. Each person changes them; the defaults: renters everything, owners new bookings, changes, payments, incidents and documents, staff requests, changes, messages and urgent alerts, field staff their jobs and pay, Admins requests, payments, messages and urgent alerts, leads and hot visitors (customer service and Sales also get the last two).</li><li>Sign-in links and codes, digests and marketing never come as alerts. An alert that is not urgent waits for the quiet hours to end for customers; an alert already read in the portal is not sent.</li><li>Your own: <b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>.</li><li>On or off for everyone: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Phone alerts&quot;.</li><li>Setup: nothing to do. The deploy makes the two keys alerts need once and keeps them; until the first deploy after this release the cards are hidden and <b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> says so. A phone that uninstalled the app or turned alerts off is removed by itself.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-lead-and-visitor-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Lead and visitor alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Staff get an alert, in the app and on their phone, for what needs a person quickly. They are never emailed or texted, so the daily email limit is untouched. The Admins always get them (every device that turned alerts on, so both of you on the shared Admin account); the rest go to the person it concerns.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">What</th><th scope="col">Who gets it</th><th scope="col">Topic</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A new renter lead: the contact form, the phone number box, a discount game claim, the live chat. It names the source.</td><td>You, and the person the lead is assigned to; if nobody, customer service and Sales on duty</td><td>Leads</td></tr><tr><td>A request typed into the booking request or contact form and not sent (after the capture delay, 30 minutes)</td><td>The same</td><td>Leads</td></tr><tr><td>A new owner lead, including &quot;Website form, unfinished&quot;, and again when an unfinished application becomes the 30-minute chase</td><td>You, and the Sales person it is assigned to</td><td>Leads</td></tr><tr><td>A visitor turns Hot on Live visitors (analytics consent only, once per visitor per day)</td><td>You, and customer service and Sales on duty</td><td>Visitors</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On duty means someone who had Live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A lead alert goes at once, at any hour, unless the person turned the <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b> topic off on that device (<b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">More than 5 lead alerts in 10 minutes become one &quot;N new leads&quot; alert for the rest of that window.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Test and verification accounts never get them, and a test address never makes one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The switches are under <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Staff alerts for leads and visitors&quot;, all on. Live visitors&#39; own &quot;notify hot&quot; switch must also be on for the hot visitor alert.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>customer service and Sales are only alerted while on duty. With nobody on duty, only the Admins are alerted; the lead is on Leads for the team in the morning.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-everything-else-that-alerts-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Everything else that alerts you</h2><p class="gd-p">Every staff alert is one rule: what happens, who gets it and a tier. Urgent: on the phone at once, at any hour. Normal: on the phone, held until the quiet hours end. Digest: a line in <b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> only. All are on. What each one is and who gets it: the chapter &quot;Alerts: the bell and your phone&quot;.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Switch a kind off or change its tier: <b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> (the bell) &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, &quot;Which alerts staff get&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The amounts and timings (a payment over $500, passing on an unopened urgent alert after 15 minutes, the briefs, grouping, complaint words): <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Staff alerts&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The App Store and Google Play links are empty until the app is published. When set, phones are asked to download the app instead of turning on browser alerts.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'alerts-the-bell-and-your-phone', 'chapter', 'text-alerts-email-text-or-both', null, 'Alerts: the bell and your phone', 'Every alert for you in one list, the buttons on a phone alert, quiet hours, focus mode, and which alerts staff get.',
  'The bell at the top of the menu opens **Alerts**: every alert for you, newest first, with the number not yet read. The same alerts reach your phone when phone alerts are on. Nothing to set up.

## The list

1. Press the bell. **All**, **Unread** or **Urgent** narrows the list.
2. Press an alert to open its page; it is marked read. **Mark read** or **Mark all read** clears without opening.
3. **Snooze 30 min** on an urgent alert: it comes again in 30 minutes and is not passed on meanwhile.

Red dot: urgent and unread. Black dot: unread.

## What alerts you

| Group | Alerts |
| --- | --- |
| Leads | New renter lead (form, phone number box, game claim, live chat), request typed and not sent, new owner lead and unfinished application, visitor turning Hot |
| Bookings | Confirmed, going out, back, closed, no-show (urgent), cancelled, offer sent, viewed, accepted and about to expire, extension asked or paid, change asked or applied, deposit released, insurer booking with no claim number |
| Money | Payment of $500 or more, refund, deposit hold failed and card declined at pickup (urgent), owner debit failed (urgent), investor money, the 9 pm cash summary |
| Field work | Job assigned, started, finished, running late (urgent), checklist incomplete, fuel or km off at return |
| Documents | Licence to review, agreement signed, agreement not signed 2 hours before pickup (urgent), insurance proof missing 24 hours before |
| Customers | Reviews (3 stars or less urgent), complaint words in chat, texts or emails, account deletion asked (urgent), unsubscribes and STOP (in Alerts only) |
| Fleet | Tracker offline, left the zone or Ontario, speeding, driving after the return time, battery (urgent), service due (in Alerts only), car paused or unpublished |
| Owners and investors | Owner gives notice (urgent), owner banking changed (urgent), investor signed |
| System | Admin sign-in from a new device or country (urgent), many failed sign-ins (urgent), deploy finished or failed, usage over 80% and data health (in Alerts only) |
| Staff and hiring | Academy lessons, quizzes failed twice, certified; Sales late or idle in their hours; new application, AI interview scored, link expired, offer accepted |
| Wins | First booking of a car, record day or week, an owner''s first payout, the month''s totals on the 1st |
| Briefs | 8 am morning brief, 9 pm evening wrap; an urgent alert nobody opened |

Also a line for each important message sent to a renter, owner or investor (late notices and the return-time notice are urgent).

## Buttons on a phone alert

- **Call**: opens your phone''s dialer with the lead''s or renter''s number (the Quo app if it handles your calls).
- **Send offer**, **Approve** or **Decline**, **Mark picked up**: open the booking where you do it. Nothing is decided from the lock screen.
- **Snooze 30 min** on urgent alerts.

## Who gets what

- Customer service, Sales and Fleet get their function''s alerts while on duty (Live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes), and what is assigned to them. Field staff get their jobs. Each gets a morning brief of their own work at 8 am.
- An urgent alert a team member did not open in 15 minutes goes to the next person on duty, then to you after another 15.
- More than 5 alerts of one kind in 10 minutes reach the phone once, as a group; each stays in the list.
- Test and verification accounts never get alerts, and a test address never makes one.

## Settings

**Alerts** > **Settings**:

1. **Phone alerts**: turn them on for this device, choose the topics, or keep a different choice on this device only.
2. **Quiet hours** (9 pm to 8 am unless you change them): normal alerts wait until they end. Urgent alerts always come.
3. **Focus mode** for 1 or 3 hours: only urgent alerts reach your phone; the rest wait in the list.
4. **Which alerts staff get**: each kind on or off, and urgent, normal or digest.

> Tip: the full table of every alert and every role is docs/alerts/matrix.md in the code.',
