k</td><td>Job assigned, started, finished, running late (urgent), checklist incomplete, fuel or km off at return</td></tr><tr><td>Documents</td><td>Licence to review, agreement signed, agreement not signed 2 hours before pickup (urgent), insurance proof missing 24 hours before</td></tr><tr><td>Customers</td><td>Reviews (3 stars or less urgent), complaint words in chat, texts or emails, account deletion asked (urgent), unsubscribes and STOP (in Alerts only)</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet</td><td>Tracker offline, left the zone or Ontario, speeding, driving after the return time, battery (urgent), service due (in Alerts only), car paused or unpublished</td></tr><tr><td>Owners and investors</td><td>Owner gives notice (urgent), owner banking changed (urgent), investor signed</td></tr><tr><td>System</td><td>Admin sign-in from a new device or country (urgent), many failed sign-ins (urgent), deploy finished or failed, usage over 80% and data health (in Alerts only)</td></tr><tr><td>Staff and hiring</td><td>Academy lessons, quizzes failed twice, certified; Sales late or idle in their hours; new application, AI interview scored, link expired, offer accepted</td></tr><tr><td>Wins</td><td>First booking of a car, record day or week, an owner&#39;s first payout, the month&#39;s totals on the 1st</td></tr><tr><td>Briefs</td><td>8 am morning brief, 9 pm evening wrap; an urgent alert nobody opened</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="gd-p">Also a line for each important message sent to a renter, owner or investor (late notices and the return-time notice are urgent).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="alerts-the-bell-and-your-phone-buttons-on-a-phone-alert" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Buttons on a phone alert</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Call</b>: opens your phone&#39;s dialer with the lead&#39;s or renter&#39;s number (the Quo app if it handles your calls).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Send offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>: open the booking where you do it. Nothing is decided from the lock screen.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Snooze 30 min</b> on urgent alerts.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="alerts-the-bell-and-your-phone-who-gets-what" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who gets what</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Customer service, Sales and Fleet get their function&#39;s alerts while on duty (Live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes), and what is assigned to them. Field staff get their jobs. Each gets a morning brief of their own work at 8 am.</li><li>An urgent alert a team member did not open in 15 minutes goes to the next person on duty, then to you after another 15.</li><li>More than 5 alerts of one kind in 10 minutes reach the phone once, as a group; each stays in the list.</li><li>Test and verification accounts never get alerts, and a test address never makes one.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="alerts-the-bell-and-your-phone-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Settings</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Phone alerts</b>: turn them on for this device, choose the topics, or keep a different choice on this device only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Quiet hours</b> (9 pm to 8 am unless you change them): normal alerts wait until they end. Urgent alerts always come.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Focus mode</b> for 1 or 3 hours: only urgent alerts reach your phone; the rest wait in the list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Which alerts staff get</b>: each kind on or off, and urgent, normal or digest.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>the full table of every alert and every role is docs/alerts/matrix.md in the code.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'live-visitors-and-live-chat', 'chapter', 'academy', 'Customer service and Sales see who is on the site now and answer the live chat. The CarmaCars assistant answers first; you take over whenever you want.

## Live visitors

1. Open **Live visitors** (customer service; Sales: **More sales**). "Live now" counts who is on the site now, "Visitors today" the people seen today. The page refreshes by itself every 15 seconds; the menu shows how many hot visitors are on the site. Each visitor shows a booking likelihood from 0 to 100 (Hot, Warm or Cold); the most likely to book come first.
2. "Why" gives the three strongest reasons, for example "Pickup tomorrow · Saw $320 for 3 days · Tapped to call". The badges are all the signals; the dots say how strong each is.
3. Each visitor shows a name when known, otherwise "Visitor from Toronto, phone", the page and car they are on, how many others look at that car now, and this visit''s pages.
4. Suggested: the next step and a message. Press **Invite to chat with this message**, or **Edit the message** first. Sales can **Offer a 10% discount code** (one per visitor a week). **Assign to Sales** hands the visitor to Sales with a task. When their dates are taken, **Suggest a similar free car** writes the message for you.
5. Press **Pages** for the whole visit. Press **Start a chat** to write your own short friendly message and press **Send**: the visitor sees it in a bubble.
6. A hot visitor raises an alert at the top of the page. Each action shows on the visitor ("Invited by Lena, 2 min ago"), so check it before writing.

## Name a visitor

When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), press **Name** on their line, type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note, then press **Save the name**. The name shows on Live visitors, Visitor history and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. Only staff see it. A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo. If they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours. **Edit name** changes it; **Remove the name** takes it off.

## Follow-ups

Signals of known visitors raise tasks on To do with what to do, for example "Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours". Call or message, then mark the task done. A task closes by itself when the renter answers or pays. Follow-ups done count in My sales.

Renters also get one polite reminder email (and at most one more) when they leave an offer, the pay page or a change unanswered. Taking the follow-up task, a chat with you or a message from you stops these reminders: you are handling it.

## Live chat

1. Open **Live chat**. The menu counts the chats that need a reply (waiting for a person, or the visitor wrote last). Reply within 5 minutes.
2. Choose a conversation. Beside it: the visitor''s page, pages and signals, and the renter''s bookings when known.
3. Press **Take over** (or just write a reply): the assistant stops. Write and press **Send** or Enter. The visitor sees when you type.
4. **Hand back to the assistant** when you are done, or **Close**. A visitor who gave an email gets a copy of the chat.
5. Each new visitor message that waits for staff sends one alert (the bell, and your phone with phone alerts on). Tick "Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)" or desktop alerts if you want them too.
6. A visitor who left the site for 10 minutes: with no phone or email the chat closes (**Visitor left, no contact**); with one it shows **Follow up by text/email** and the task is in your queue. Text or email them, then mark the task done. If they come back, the chat opens again.
7. **AI replies paused** at the top says why the assistant is not answering; a staff note in the chat says the same. Answer the visitor yourself.

> Tip: Prices: send a quote from New quote, never a price from memory. If you handled the chat, choose "I sourced this client" on the quote; nothing is credited by itself.

## Alerts on your phone

With phone alerts on (**Profile** > **Phone alerts**) you get an alert, in the app and on your phone, for:

- A new lead assigned to you, or, when nobody has it, any new lead while you are on duty (live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes): contact form, phone number box, discount game claim or live chat. The alert names the source.
- A request someone typed into the booking request or contact form and did not send.
- A new owner lead assigned to you, if you are in Sales, and the unfinished application that became a lead to chase.
- A visitor turning Hot on Live visitors, while you are on duty.

1. Open the alert to land on Leads, Owner pipeline or Live visitors.
2. Call or text the person first; the task closes by itself when they send the form.
3. Too many? Turn **Leads** or **Visitors** off for a device on the same card. Bursts of more than 5 in 10 minutes arrive as one "N new leads" alert.

> Tip: Lead alerts come at any hour, so set your phone''s own quiet hours for the night.
