## Alerts on your phone

The bell at the top of the menu opens **Alerts**, the list of everything for you; the same alerts reach your phone once phone alerts are on (**Alerts** > **Settings**). You get:

- A new lead assigned to you, or, when nobody has it, any new lead while you are on duty (live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes): contact form, phone number box, discount game claim or live chat. The alert names the source.
- A request someone typed into the booking request or contact form and did not send.
- A new owner lead assigned to you, if you are in Sales, and the unfinished application that became a lead to chase.
- A visitor turning Hot on Live visitors, while you are on duty.
- Your function''s alerts while on duty: customer service the licences to review, complaint words, agreements not signed 2 hours before pickup and insurance proof missing; Sales offers about to expire; Fleet cars going out and back, no-shows, cancellations, cards declined at pickup and the tracker alerts.
- An urgent alert a colleague did not open in 15 minutes ("Passed to you").
- A morning brief at 8 am of your own work.

1. Open the alert to land on its page. **Call** on the phone alert opens your dialer with the number; **Send offer**, **Approve** or **Decline** open the booking.
2. Call or text the person first; the task closes by itself when they send the form.
3. Too many? In **Alerts** > **Settings** turn a topic off, set your quiet hours (normal alerts wait until they end), or turn on focus mode (only urgent ones for 1 or 3 hours). Bursts arrive as one alert.
4. **Snooze 30 min** on an urgent alert brings it back in 30 minutes; it is not passed on meanwhile.

> Tip: urgent alerts come at any hour, whatever your quiet hours.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Customer service and Sales see who is on the site now and answer the live chat. The CarmaCars assistant answers first; you take over whenever you want.</p><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-live-visitors" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Live visitors</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Live visitors</b> (customer service; Sales: <b class="gd-ui">More sales</b>). &quot;Live now&quot; counts who is on the site now, &quot;Visitors today&quot; the people seen today. The page refreshes by itself every 15 seconds; the menu shows how many hot visitors are on the site. Each visitor shows a booking likelihood from 0 to 100 (Hot, Warm or Cold); the most likely to book come first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Why&quot; gives the three strongest reasons, for example &quot;Pickup tomorrow · Saw $320 for 3 days · Tapped to call&quot;. The badges are all the signals; the dots say how strong each is.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each visitor shows a name when known, otherwise &quot;Visitor from Toronto, phone&quot;, the page and car they are on, how many others look at that car now, and this visit&#39;s pages.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Suggested: the next step and a message. Press <b class="gd-ui">Invite to chat with this message</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Edit the message</b> first. Sales can <b class="gd-ui">Offer a 10% discount code</b> (one per visitor a week). <b class="gd-ui">Assign to Sales</b> hands the visitor to Sales with a task. When their dates are taken, <b class="gd-ui">Suggest a similar free car</b> writes the message for you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Pages</b> for the whole visit. Press <b class="gd-ui">Start a chat</b> to write your own short friendly message and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>: the visitor sees it in a bubble.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A hot visitor raises an alert at the top of the page. Each action shows on the visitor (&quot;Invited by Lena, 2 min ago&quot;), so check it before writing.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-name-a-visitor" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Name a visitor</h2><p class="gd-p">When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), press <b class="gd-ui">Name</b> on their line, type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note, then press <b class="gd-ui">Save the name</b>. The name shows on Live visitors, Visitor history and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. Only staff see it. A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo. If they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours. <b class="gd-ui">Edit name</b> changes it; <b class="gd-ui">Remove the name</b> takes it off.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-follow-ups" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Follow-ups</h2><p class="gd-p">Signals of known visitors raise tasks on To do with what to do, for example &quot;Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours&quot;. Call or message, then mark the task done. A task closes by itself when the renter answers or pays. Follow-ups done count in My sales.</p><p class="gd-p">Renters also get one polite reminder email (and at most one more) when they leave an offer, the pay page or a change unanswered. Taking the follow-up task, a chat with you or a message from you stops these reminders: you are handling it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-live-chat" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Live chat</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Live chat</b>. The menu counts the chats that need a reply (waiting for a person, or the visitor wrote last). Reply within 5 minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a conversation. Beside it: the visitor&#39;s page, pages and signals, and the renter&#39;s bookings when known.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take over</b> (or just write a reply): the assistant stops. Write and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b> or Enter. The visitor sees when you type.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hand back to the assistant</b> when you are done, or <b class="gd-ui">Close</b>. A visitor who gave an email gets a copy of the chat.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Each new visitor message that waits for staff sends one alert (the bell, and your phone with phone alerts on). Tick &quot;Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)&quot; or desktop alerts if you want them too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A visitor who left the site for 10 minutes: with no phone or email the chat closes (<b class="gd-ui">Visitor left, no contact</b>); with one it shows <b class="gd-ui">Follow up by text/email</b> and the task is in your queue. Text or email them, then mark the task done. If they come back, the chat opens again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">AI replies paused</b> at the top says why the assistant is not answering; a staff note in the chat says the same. Answer the visitor yourself.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Prices: send a quote from New quote, never a price from memory. If you handled the chat, choose &quot;I sourced this client&quot; on the quote; nothing is credited by itself.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-alerts-on-your-phone" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Alerts on your phone</h2><p class="gd-p">The bell at the top of the menu opens <b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b>, the list of everything for you; the same alerts reach your phone once phone alerts are on (<b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>). You get:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A new lead assigned to you, or, when nobody has it, any new lead while you are on duty (live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes): contact form, phone number box, discount game claim or live chat. The alert names the source.</li><li>A request someone typed into the booking request or contact form and did not send.</li><li>A new owner lead assigned to you, if you are in Sales, and the unfinished application that became a lead to chase.</li><li>A visitor turning Hot on Live visitors, while you are on duty.</li><li>Your function&#39;s alerts while on duty: customer service the licences to review, complaint words, agreements not signed 2 hours before pickup and insurance proof missing; Sales offers about to expire; Fleet cars going out and back, no-shows, cancellations, cards declined at pickup and the tracker alerts.</li><li>An urgent alert a colleague did not open in 15 minutes (&quot;Passed to you&quot;).</li><li>A morning brief at 8 am of your own work.</li></ul><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the alert to land on its page. <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on the phone alert opens your dialer with the number; <b class="gd-ui">Send offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> open the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Call or text the person first; the task closes by itself when they send the form.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Too many? In <b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> turn a topic off, set your quiet hours (normal alerts wait until they end), or turn on focus mode (only urgent ones for 1 or 3 hours). Bursts arrive as one alert.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Snooze 30 min</b> on an urgent alert brings it back in 30 minutes; it is not passed on meanwhile.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>urgent alerts come at any hour, whatever your quiet hours.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'report-rentals-referrals-and-profile', 'chapter', 'academy', 'Report anything that happens on the road, add a rental for a renter you found, share your referral link, and keep your details up to date.

## Report a problem

1. Open **Report a problem** and choose the Car.
2. Choose What happened: **New damage found**, **Warning light**, **Collision while I was driving**, **Ticket or toll while I was driving**, **Lost property found** or **Something else**.
3. Write the Details: where, when and what you see.
4. Press **Take a photo** for each photo, then **Send the report**.

![](/guides/img/field-03-report-phone-3b903b20.jpg "phone; size: 390 1040; pins: 1 93.6 46.6, 2 93.6 64.9, 3 93.6 89.9")

> Watch out: In a collision, make sure everyone is safe and call 911 if anyone is hurt. Then call CarmaCars at 289-312-5991 before you send the report.

## Add a rental for a renter you found

Your home address must be in your profile first: until it is, the page asks for it.

1. Open **Add a rental**. Choose the car, the dates and the places, then type the renter''s details. A renter already on file is found by their email. Car already out with the renter? Enter the pickup as when it left: it is recorded as on trip.
2. Press **Check the calendar and the price**. To charge another price, type it with the reason: a price far under the rate sheet is flagged for an Admin, not refused.
3. Choose **Send a payment link** or **Charge the saved card when the renter signs**. The renter pays online: you take no payment for it yourself.
4. Under Who found this client, choose **I sourced this client** or **Entered for CarmaCars**, then press **Add the rental**.

## Commissions

1. You earn 10% of the rental charge (before tax, after discounts, less refunds) of each rental you sourced: one you added and marked I sourced this client, or a booking made with your referral link.
2. It is earned when the rental is completed and paid in full, then an Admin approves it and it is paid on your pay date. Your home address must be in your profile: until it is, a commission waits as not earned yet.
3. **My sales** shows each commission: not earned yet, pending approval, approved, paid or reversed. A refund after payment comes off a later commission.

## Referrals and profile

1. **Referrals**: your own referral link. Press **Copy the link**, or let someone scan its QR code. A booking made with it counts as a rental you sourced.
2. **Profile**: **Save my phone**, your home address (**Change my home address**), **Set up two-step sign-in**, **Change my password** and **Sign out**.

![](/guides/img/field-04-profile-phone-f05000e2.jpg "phone; size: 390 920; pins: 2 92.3 78.3")

## Sign in with your phone number

Quicker on a phone than a password: a 6-digit code by text.

1. On **Profile**, under Sign-in, press **Add and verify my phone number**, enter your mobile number and press **Text me a code**.
2. Type the code from the text (it usually fills itself in) and press **Verify**. Choose **My phone number (a code by text)** under Sign in with.
3. Next time, the sign-in page opens on your phone number: press **Text me a code** and enter the code. Two-step sign-in still asks for your authenticator code.

## Texts or email

On **Profile**, under **Messages**, choose **Email**, **Text** or **Both** for the messages we send you. Texts need the phone you verified above.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert the moment a job is assigned to you or changes, and when you are paid. Open **Profile**, press **Turn on alerts** under **Phone alerts** and allow notifications. On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**) and turn alerts on from there.
